{
	title: 'Icon candidates demo page',
	spec: 'src/web/demo/icons.html, served at /demo/icons, compares fifteen candidate web-client icons (send, attach, image, python, thinking, download, copy, bash, read file, edit file, edit/pencil, web, pause/continue, steer, queue) across seven free sets: Lucide (ISC), Phosphor, Tabler, Hugeicons free, Fluent UI System Icons, Boxicons (MIT) and MingCute (Apache 2.0). Licence notices sit in page source; no attribution shows to users. Lucide, Phosphor and Tabler SVGs come from their repos; the others from the Iconify JSON packages. The user switches set (also via #lucide, #hugeicons and so on), stroke and size; the size slider (12–48px) scales every icon, and stroke affects line-drawn sets only. Pickers choose the thinking icon (real thought bubble by default, only in Hugeicons, Fluent, Boxicons and MingCute; light bulb, sparkle, chat bubble, ellipsis, atom, brain), steer icon, queue icon attach icon (paper clip by default, or image plus) and Python icon (snakes from IconPark, Pinhead and Material Design Icons, shown in every set because none of the seven has one; Python logo from Tabler and Hugeicons), remembered in localStorage. A dashed box marks an icon a set lacks. Samples show composers (including pause, queue and steer while a turn runs) and transcript cards in the real theme colours, with a pencil edit button on a sent prompt. Icon-only buttons carry aria-labels. The page is a design aid; adopting icons in the client is a separate decision.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Icon data in icons.html is generated: one key table maps each icon to its name per set, and the SVG bodies are inlined as one JSON line (ICONS) plus NAMES. Iconify API search rate-limits quickly (HTTP 429); the jsdelivr @iconify-json/<prefix>/icons.json packages carry the same data without limits. Lucide, Phosphor and Tabler lack a true thought bubble (their chat bubbles with dots read as messaging).',
		'The thinking picker also offers bubbles (Hugeicons MIT, Lucide ISC) and flasks (Phosphor MIT, Iconoir round-flask MIT), shown in every set. Borrowed 24-grid stroke icons carry class g24 so the Phosphor sets 256-grid stroke scaling does not swell them into solid blobs.'
